stage_b_summary:
Stage B for microsoft/rushstack@a1d41fc46f. Stage A's config is sound: validate-config loads 66 rules, and check exits rc=0 on the clone and on a scratch copy. Every locale, dep-version and toolchain-pin unit with a rule fired when I broke it on a scratch copy (toolchain-pin A units 05, 07 and 52; dep-version C units 03 and 04), and other-family spot checks fired too.

The main completeness gap is Rush's CommandLineConfiguration loader. Beyond the schema, it validates:
- phase-name syntax (b01);
- unique phase and command names (b02, B-config unique-key);
- that every referenced phase exists (b03, A, four cross_file rules);
- parameter associatedCommands (b04, C);
- that ignoreMissingScript and missingScriptBehavior are exclusive (b05);
- that build and rebuild are not global (b06);
- that phase self-dependencies have no cycle (b07, B-kernel);
- that custom commands do not reuse built-in action names (b08, C);
- that autoinstallers resolve (b09, C).

Stage A covered only the globalPlugin rejection, and under the wrong unit label (09b).

Other missed units:
- rig.json load validation (b10, A, fire-verified), which Stage A lumped into D unit 46;
- the static validity of nodeSupportedVersionRange as a semver range (b11, toolchain-pin, B-adapter; the one missed unit in a target family);
- package-name keys in common-versions.json (b12, C);
- the registry= line that the release pipeline requires in .npmrc-publish (b13, A);
- heft-plugin.json schema validation (b14, A);
- three schema files the 09 rule set leaves out (b15; by R1 they belong to 09).

Suggested reclassifications:
- rushstack-10 to C: it hardcodes depth 2.
- rushstack-46: narrow it, since rig.json validation is A.
- rushstack-47 from D to B-config unique-key: the remainder needs no build.

Config issues:
- rule 07 lacks if_present;
- rule 03 over-asserts on alias, tag, file and catalog specifiers;
- rule 57 misses the default subspace folder;
- rule 23 is case-sensitive where Rush is not.

Nothing to remove.

Not units:
- The .npmignore 'DO NOT MODIFY ABOVE THIS LINE' template is violated at the pin by rush-plugins/rush-published-versions-json-plugin/.npmignore (R5).
- The copilot, trae and cursor rule files carry generic Rush advice.
- common/config/rush-plugins/rush-serve-plugin.json configures a plugin that rush-plugins.json does not list, so it is dead config.
- catalogs appear only in rush-lib test fixtures.

The scratch directory is removed.
